{"c":[{"id":"60b138f01f887219","sum":"T1: compare field values with .utf16.elementsEqual or digests, never Swift String == (canonical equivalence lets é match e+U+0301); NSSpellChecker's orthography option is only a starting point under automatic language (French passes under en).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T170510Z-7982a134da3a9b97","text":"Swift String == is canonical equivalence (precomposed é equals e+U+0301): guards comparing field values must use .utf16.elementsEqual or digests, or a normalizing app passes a mismatched write (T1 RangeEdit.verify).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T170510Z-ca62d5f751cbf8cc","text":"NSSpellChecker requestChecking treats the orthography option as a starting point: with the system's automatic language on, French text passes under en and tres passes under fr (T1, macOS 26.6).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b105c8e9d793ad2e","sum":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true is the host (v2/host must send it or no skill runs on its own; evals call helper.hostConnected); forward writes carry a mark, undo sends sameAs, the reader answers notSameElement for any other element (fakes: test/fake-marks.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-0e49751b5685c975","text":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true counts as the host; other consumers bind their own work but keep no run with no Tab alive. v2/host must send host: true, or no skill runs on its own. In-process evals still call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-101e1e3d273eec2a","text":"B23: forward value writes carry a mark and undo sends sameAs; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element at the key is the one it wrote (per app worker, gone on reader restart). Test fakes use test/fake-marks.ts; marks.replace(windowId, key) plays a replaced field.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
